# .env.staging — for `./setup-zitadel.sh --target staging` (and --target staging
# on setup-openfga.sh).
#
# READ THIS FIRST: staging is NOT a separate instance. It is the PRODUCTION
# Zitadel/OpenFGA at auth.catholicdigitalcommons.org, carrying the staging
# origin set. `--target` selects which APP and which origins a run touches, not
# which server it talks to. That is why every endpoint below is identical to
# .env.production's.
#
# Consequence worth internalising before you run anything: the only thing
# separating a staging run from a production run is the --target flag. Both
# reach the same instance with the same credentials.
#
# WHY THIS FILE CARRIES NO SECRETS
#
# setup-zitadel.sh reads exactly the three variables below. It does NOT read
# the DB passwords, ZITADEL_MASTERKEY, admin password, OPENFGA_PRESHARED_KEY or
# SMTP settings that .env.production carries — those are for `docker compose`,
# which only ever runs with --env-file .env.production. Copying them here would
# double their exposure and buy nothing.
#
# So: copy this file, do not copy .env.production.
#
#   sudo install -o ubuntu -g ubuntu -m 600 \
#       /opt/cdcf-auth/auth/.env.staging.example \
#       /opt/cdcf-auth/auth/.env.staging
#
# Ownership matters: the provisioning scripts run as ubuntu, while the repo
# checkout is owned by cdcfinfra-deploy, so ubuntu cannot create files in
# auth/ without sudo. Mode 0600 and ubuntu ownership match .env.production.
#
# The three values below are also the scripts' built-in defaults, so an empty
# file would work today. They are set explicitly anyway, so that a future change
# to those defaults cannot silently repoint a staging run at something else.

ZITADEL_ISSUER=https://auth.catholicdigitalcommons.org
ZITADEL_INTERNAL_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
ZITADEL_PAT_FILE=/opt/cdcf-auth/runtime/zitadel-data/automation-user.pat
